WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.209
Reading day two's drift, the three credentials
the rule couldn't see are all there:

2
00:00:05.209 --> 00:00:09.898
one added by a person, one added by
another app abusing a broad permission,

3
00:00:09.898 --> 00:00:12.087
and the very first secret on an app.

4
00:00:12.087 --> 00:00:16.480
Just as important is what's missing:
the pipeline's own two rotations,

5
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.538
because both the identity
and the key log agree.

6
00:00:19.538 --> 00:00:23.751
An expiring certificate from day
one is gone, because it was rotated.

7
00:00:23.751 --> 00:00:27.075
A chapter file with a forged
fingerprint is refused.

8
00:00:27.075 --> 00:00:31.665
Then the vintage comparison finds a
new deployed agent with no identity,

9
00:00:31.665 --> 00:00:34.780
and a retired use case
whose app is still enabled.
